Models differ in width, so compare them at the same *fraction* of their dims: 1/3, 1/6 and 1/12. Four models:

- the NLI standard model and its Matryoshka twin (768 dims, trained on NLI sentence pairs);
- **all-MiniLM-L6-v2** (384 dims), trained with no Matryoshka loss on over a billion mixed pairs (Reddit replies, question-answer, query-passage and citation pairs);
- **nomic-embed-text-v1.5** (768 dims), trained with Matryoshka on retrieval pairs: its card describes a contrastive stage on weakly related text pairs, then fine-tuning on labeled data. Prefixes `search_query: ` and `search_document: `, layer norm, slice, L2-normalize, as the card says.

blocks.code:
CREATE TABLE docs (id bigint PRIMARY KEY, embedding vector(768));

CREATE INDEX ON docs USING hnsw
  ((subvector(embedding, 1, 256)::vector(256)) vector_cosine_ops);

-- $1 is the layer-normed 768-d query vector
SELECT id FROM (
  SELECT id, embedding FROM docs
  ORDER BY subvector(embedding, 1, 256)::vector(256)
           <=> subvector($1::vector, 1, 256)
  LIMIT 100                                   -- stage 1: K = 100
) AS shortlist
ORDER BY embedding <=> $1::vector             -- stage 2: full vector
LIMIT 10;
